  "decision_date": "22/07/2002",
  "description": "Change of use of ground floor to A3 use, erection of first floor rear extension, erection of a fourth and part fifth floor and conversion of the upper floors to five one bed flats and four two bed flats.",
  "site_name": "101 - 105",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "21/11/2001",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "21/07/2005",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before any part of the building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - The premises shall not be used for the sale of food or drink for consumption off the premises other than confectionery.",
    "Condition : 5 - The use hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the hours of 0800 to 2300.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - The uses as A3 with flats above hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing and collection of refuse or waste, and details of loading and servicing, have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing and collection of refuse or waste, and servicing and loading, shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and refuse storage shall completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 8 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external noise shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 9 - The building shall be constructed and adapted so as to provide sound insulation against internally generated noise between the restaurant andthe flats, and between the flats themselves, of not less than 30dB(A) with windows shut and other means of ventilation provided.",
    "Condition : 10 - The use shall not commence until a scheme for the ventilation of the premises of an appropriate outlet level, including details of sound attenuation for any necessary plant and the standard or dilution expected has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 11 - Before the development hereby permitted is commenced a scheme indicating the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to the A3 unit and the flats above shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use."
  ],
